1
00:01:32,930 --> 00:01:35,050
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:37,680
[Episode 15]

3
00:01:41,039 --> 00:01:41,789
Come on.

4
00:01:42,150 --> 00:01:42,950
Come on in.

5
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:46,509
This is our office.

6
00:01:47,509 --> 00:01:48,710
And here is your seat.

7
00:01:52,759 --> 00:01:54,690
My wife sewed that cushion for you,

8
00:01:54,950 --> 00:01:58,080
meaning to keep you warm,
since you're a female comrade.

9
00:01:58,280 --> 00:01:59,080
Goji berries,

10
00:01:59,590 --> 00:02:00,920
a local specialty here.

11
00:02:01,710 --> 00:02:03,310
When you steep them in water,

12
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:04,950
add a few pieces of rock sugar.

13
00:02:04,950 --> 00:02:05,950
The taste is good.

14
00:02:05,950 --> 00:02:07,680
They also benefit the stomach.

15
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:08,830
Thanks, Mentor.

16
00:02:09,250 --> 00:02:10,630
But don't you worry about me.

17
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:12,090
I'm actually quite tough.

18
00:02:12,750 --> 00:02:13,360
Really?

19
00:02:14,030 --> 00:02:14,560
Alright.

20
00:02:16,710 --> 00:02:18,150
Let's go check out the dorm.

21
00:02:18,150 --> 00:02:18,579
Sure.

22
00:02:18,630 --> 00:02:19,060
Okay.

23
00:02:19,150 --> 00:02:19,880
Come with me.

24
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:22,610
Here.

25
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:24,190
Come this way.

26
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:26,700
Mentor.

27
00:02:27,630 --> 00:02:29,360
Is the prison break real?

28
00:02:31,430 --> 00:02:32,960
Don't scare yourself.

29
00:02:33,430 --> 00:02:34,690
It's pretty safe here.

30
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:35,760
Prison break?

31
00:02:35,910 --> 00:02:38,120
There hasn't been one such incident here.

32
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:39,280
Look at this place.

33
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:42,040
Can escapees possibly get away?

34
00:02:43,590 --> 00:02:44,520
This is the dorm.

35
00:02:45,590 --> 00:02:47,450
But usually nobody lives in there.

36
00:02:47,450 --> 00:02:48,930
You see, the downtown

37
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:50,280
is 50 kilometers away.

38
00:02:50,710 --> 00:02:52,690
There are shuttle buses for commuting.

39
00:02:52,690 --> 00:02:53,360
After work,

40
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:55,190
staffers would rather take the bus home

41
00:02:55,190 --> 00:02:57,120
and return early the next morning.

42
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:57,930
Oh right.

43
00:02:58,710 --> 00:02:59,750
This is the restroom.

44
00:02:59,750 --> 00:03:00,120
Look,

45
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:01,240
here.

46
00:03:01,370 --> 00:03:02,920
It's a public restroom.

47
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:04,840
Remember,

48
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:06,780
take a flashlight with you

49
00:03:06,870 --> 00:03:08,000
when you go at night,

50
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:09,520
so you won't fall,

51
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:11,450
as this is a dry toilet.

52
00:03:11,610 --> 00:03:12,080
Besides,

53
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:13,280
that's the washroom.

54
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:15,490
Feel free to do your washing

55
00:03:15,590 --> 00:03:16,400
right there.

56
00:03:18,310 --> 00:03:19,560
Be careful with this.

57
00:03:19,590 --> 00:03:20,870
Try not to let the oil drip on you.

58
00:03:20,870 --> 00:03:22,400
It doesn't wash off easily.

59
00:03:23,310 --> 00:03:24,170
Please come in.

60
00:03:25,590 --> 00:03:26,590
You'll stay here.

61
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:29,490
I've got you some hot water.

62
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:32,170
My room is right next door.

63
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:33,030
If you need help,

64
00:03:33,030 --> 00:03:34,329
just knock on the wall

65
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:35,360
like this.

66
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:36,540
I'll try not to.

67
00:03:37,150 --> 00:03:37,910
It's okay.

68
00:03:38,790 --> 00:03:40,430
Alright. Sort your things out

69
00:03:40,430 --> 00:03:41,430
and get some rest.

70
00:03:41,470 --> 00:03:42,670
If you need anything,

71
00:03:42,870 --> 00:03:43,840
just let me know.

72
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:46,300
Thank you, Mentor.

73
00:03:46,310 --> 00:03:47,510
Forgo the formality.

74
00:04:15,910 --> 00:04:16,570
Is it heavy?

75
00:04:16,610 --> 00:04:17,339
I can manage.

76
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:18,420
Mom, let me take it.

77
00:04:18,750 --> 00:04:19,070
Mom.

78
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:20,269
Let's just go.

79
00:04:20,269 --> 00:04:20,600
Go.

80
00:04:20,630 --> 00:04:21,040
Yu,

81
00:04:21,269 --> 00:04:22,600
are your family visiting?

82
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:23,720
A co-worker of mine.

83
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:24,430
Hello, Mr. Yu, Mrs. Yu.

84
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:24,830
Hello.

85
00:04:24,850 --> 00:04:25,980
I'll leave you to it.

86
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:32,100
This is it, my room.

87
00:04:35,830 --> 00:04:36,430
Here it is.

88
00:04:37,159 --> 00:04:37,620
Come on.

89
00:04:42,310 --> 00:04:43,310
Give it to me, Mom.

90
00:04:45,750 --> 00:04:46,360
Come on in.

91
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:48,159
Here, Mom.

92
00:04:53,720 --> 00:04:54,380
Have a seat.

93
00:04:55,390 --> 00:04:56,390
Dad, sit down too.

94
00:04:58,120 --> 00:04:58,650
Gaoyuan.

95
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:00,560
Is this your uniform?

96
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:01,360
Yes.

97
00:05:01,630 --> 00:05:02,680
I wear it to court.

98
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:05,800
Mom, have some water.

99
00:05:06,430 --> 00:05:07,230
Are you tired?

100
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:08,480
No, not at all.

101
00:05:09,020 --> 00:05:10,480
We sat on these two bags all the way here.

102
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:11,160
It was cozy.

103
00:05:11,390 --> 00:05:13,270
Didn't I ask you to buy sleeper tickets?

104
00:05:13,270 --> 00:05:15,000
Why standing tickets instead?

105
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,430
Did I not send home enough money?

106
00:05:17,430 --> 00:05:18,680
You did. It was enough.

107
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:19,650
Sleeper tickets are hard to buy.

108
00:05:19,650 --> 00:05:20,530
Why the hassle?

109
00:05:21,050 --> 00:05:22,160
Plus, it's not easy for you

110
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:23,220
to make money here.

111
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:26,510
Put it on now.

112
00:05:26,950 --> 00:05:27,950
I'd like to see you in it.

113
00:05:27,950 --> 00:05:29,410
I'm not wearing it in here.

114
00:05:29,850 --> 00:05:30,480
Just put it on.

115
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:31,210
It's too hot in here.

116
00:05:31,210 --> 00:05:32,140
Mom, talk to him.

117
00:05:32,390 --> 00:05:33,800
I want to see you in it. Put it on.

118
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:34,380
Now!

119
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:36,650
Be good and do it.

120
00:05:37,310 --> 00:05:38,480
Fine. I'll put it on.

121
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:44,850
Help me with it, Dad.

122
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:52,270
Look, my love.

123
00:05:52,870 --> 00:05:54,330
Our boy is successful now.

124
00:05:55,310 --> 00:05:56,830
I'm taking it off. It's too hot.

125
00:05:56,830 --> 00:05:58,240
You had us hurry over.

126
00:05:58,270 --> 00:05:59,360
Is there a matter?

127
00:05:59,560 --> 00:06:00,490
Dad, take a seat.

128
00:06:04,240 --> 00:06:06,100
I mean to let you meet some people.

129
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:07,270
What people?

130
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:10,980
I'm dating someone

131
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:18,150
with a view to marriage.

132
00:06:18,150 --> 00:06:18,920
So I asked you

133
00:06:18,950 --> 00:06:20,750
to come meet her and her family.

134
00:06:24,890 --> 00:06:28,990
[Binjiang Intermediate People's Court]

135
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:27,180
The car's not here yet.

136
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:29,890
Going out to work?

137
00:06:29,890 --> 00:06:30,620
Director Ma.

138
00:06:34,950 --> 00:06:35,480
Yu.

139
00:06:35,960 --> 00:06:36,480
Yes?

140
00:06:41,190 --> 00:06:42,320
You seeing someone?

141
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:44,680
Who told you that?

142
00:06:45,240 --> 00:06:46,870
Many people saw you and Fang Haohao

143
00:06:46,870 --> 00:06:48,270
at the municipal government

144
00:06:48,270 --> 00:06:49,270
family compound.

145
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:51,020
The girl

146
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:52,800
with a bad leg, right?

147
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:56,470
She was once

148
00:06:56,560 --> 00:06:57,480
an intern here.

149
00:06:58,480 --> 00:06:59,240
Listen,

150
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:00,830
have confidence in yourself.

151
00:07:00,830 --> 00:07:02,360
People say that she's out of your league,

152
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:04,020
but I'd say it's unfair to you.

153
00:07:04,390 --> 00:07:05,440
Out of my league? How so?

154
00:07:05,440 --> 00:07:06,600
Yeah. That's so not true.

155
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:08,560
I think it's you who's too good for her.

156
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:11,090
You're an outstanding young lad,
aren't you?

157
00:07:15,830 --> 00:07:16,490
Ignore her.

158
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:20,270
What a gossipy snob.

159
00:07:21,010 --> 00:07:22,160
She's just
the canteen purchasing director,

160
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:24,220
yet she acts as if she's a real leader.

161
00:07:24,390 --> 00:07:24,680
Wait,

162
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:26,080
what did she mean by that?

163
00:07:26,310 --> 00:07:28,510
Just an insinuation
about Fang Haohao's father.

164
00:07:28,510 --> 00:07:29,840
What's with her father?

165
00:07:30,070 --> 00:07:30,930
You don't know?

166
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:32,310
Drop the act already.

167
00:07:32,310 --> 00:07:33,040
Just tell me.

168
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:35,680
Her father is a high-ranking official,

169
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:38,520
the deputy commander of a military region,

170
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:39,810
named Fang Leiming.

171
00:07:52,020 --> 00:07:53,120
What's wrong with your kid?

172
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:53,630
Yeah. What is it with him?

173
00:07:53,630 --> 00:07:55,020
Our shop has been open
for only a few days.

174
00:07:55,020 --> 00:07:55,510
Right.

175
00:07:55,510 --> 00:07:56,070
Such

176
00:07:56,070 --> 00:07:56,830
ill-bred scum.

177
00:07:56,830 --> 00:07:57,430
Excuse me.

178
00:07:58,159 --> 00:07:58,510
Let me through.

179
00:07:58,510 --> 00:07:59,480
Officer, you be the judge.

180
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:00,210
Chief Zhang.

181
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:02,430
We devoted our lives to this shop.

182
00:08:02,430 --> 00:08:03,360
What's going on?

183
00:08:03,830 --> 00:08:04,830
The same old strife.

184
00:08:04,830 --> 00:08:06,090
It just keeps on and on.

185
00:08:06,270 --> 00:08:07,160
Look at that.

186
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:09,190
It's Sun Rong's eldest son's doing.

187
00:08:09,190 --> 00:08:10,270
He poured kerosene in broad daylight

188
00:08:10,270 --> 00:08:11,670
and set the place on fire.

189
00:08:11,830 --> 00:08:12,810
I don't even dare to imagine.

190
00:08:12,810 --> 00:08:13,720
See, the shop's surrounded

191
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:14,320
by houses.

192
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:15,260
If the fire had spread,

193
00:08:15,260 --> 00:08:15,950
many people would've died.

194
00:08:15,950 --> 00:08:16,390
Right.

195
00:08:18,070 --> 00:08:19,720
Sun Rong insisted that we call you,

196
00:08:19,720 --> 00:08:21,360
saying that he knows you
and you have authority.

197
00:08:21,360 --> 00:08:22,020
I told him it was

198
00:08:22,020 --> 00:08:23,560
no use asking you to come over,

199
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:24,890
but he wouldn't listen.

200
00:08:25,270 --> 00:08:26,200
He's over there.

201
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:28,040
Got it. I'll go take a look.

202
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:28,370
Okay.

203
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:29,870
Sun.

204
00:08:29,890 --> 00:08:30,890
Prosecutor Chen!

205
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:32,039
Prosecutor Chen,

206
00:08:32,110 --> 00:08:33,039
you must help me.

207
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:33,870
You must help me.

208
00:08:33,870 --> 00:08:34,309
Get up.

209
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:35,000
My son...

210
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:37,820
My son is not even 14 years old yet.

211
00:08:38,909 --> 00:08:40,770
Nothing bad should happen to him.

212
00:08:44,030 --> 00:08:45,630
Why didn't you keep watch on him?

213
00:08:45,630 --> 00:08:46,830
I tried, but I failed.

214
00:08:47,390 --> 00:08:48,320
My son...

215
00:08:49,650 --> 00:08:51,650
did that out of hatred.

216
00:09:05,390 --> 00:09:06,630
I heard Wang Youxi's shop was burned

217
00:09:06,630 --> 00:09:08,560
soon after it reopened. Is it true?

218
00:09:09,910 --> 00:09:11,370
Yes, Sun Rong's son did it.

219
00:09:13,770 --> 00:09:15,440
What the Wangs did to that child

220
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:18,100
really left a mark in his heart,
don't you think?

221
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:19,980
Wang Youxi and his wife must be

222
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:21,330
sentenced harshly.

223
00:09:23,120 --> 00:09:24,580
Where does that come from?

224
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:25,670
The harm caused

225
00:09:25,670 --> 00:09:27,170
by Wang Youxi to Sun Rong's family

226
00:09:27,170 --> 00:09:28,390
is not a one-time thing.

227
00:09:28,390 --> 00:09:30,150
The influence continues.

228
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:31,930
Even to this day,

229
00:09:32,270 --> 00:09:34,370
Sun Rong's family are still being hurt

230
00:09:34,370 --> 00:09:35,240
psychologically

231
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:36,960
and in their daily lives.

232
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:38,520
What about the Wangs?

233
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:40,000
Their shop reopened

234
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:41,290
and they started a new life.

235
00:09:41,290 --> 00:09:42,200
What should they have

236
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:43,660
gone for, if not a new life?

237
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:45,390
Is starting a new life

238
00:09:45,390 --> 00:09:46,720
equal to another crime?

239
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:48,670
They should've taken a proper attitude,

240
00:09:48,670 --> 00:09:49,630
admitted their guilt,

241
00:09:49,630 --> 00:09:50,690
felt some remorse,

242
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:53,050
and offered compensation, right?

243
00:09:53,150 --> 00:09:54,150
But what have they done now?

244
00:09:54,150 --> 00:09:55,390
Not only have they done none of that,

245
00:09:55,390 --> 00:09:57,220
but they also don't think they are wrong.

246
00:09:57,220 --> 00:09:58,080
Isn't reopening the shop

247
00:09:58,080 --> 00:09:59,020
a way to earn money

248
00:09:59,020 --> 00:10:00,820
so they can compensate the Suns?

249
00:10:02,340 --> 00:10:02,840
Mentor, if...

250
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:04,170
if you put it that way...

251
00:10:04,270 --> 00:10:06,270
You think I'm trying to
smooth things over, right?

252
00:10:06,270 --> 00:10:07,670
If Wang Youxi and his wife are not

253
00:10:07,670 --> 00:10:09,070
given a severe sentence,

254
00:10:09,670 --> 00:10:10,720
Sun Rong's family

255
00:10:10,750 --> 00:10:11,930
will lose faith

256
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:13,160
in judicial justice.

257
00:10:13,550 --> 00:10:14,200
From here on out,

258
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:16,320
they won't believe in the law anymore.

259
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:17,980
Besides, now, Sun's son is not

260
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:19,510
even 14 years old yet.

261
00:10:19,510 --> 00:10:21,120
What if he goes down the path

262
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:21,570
of crime?

263
00:10:21,570 --> 00:10:23,630
His whole life will be ruined, right?

264
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:25,810
Wang Youxi's child is only 8 years old.

265
00:10:25,810 --> 00:10:26,840
Yes. And the Wang family

266
00:10:26,840 --> 00:10:28,370
drove the Sun family crazy.

267
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:30,840
The former was not even mistreated.

268
00:10:36,970 --> 00:10:37,910
The trial is the day after tomorrow.

269
00:10:37,910 --> 00:10:38,840
Have you decided

270
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:39,910
to still suggest

271
00:10:39,910 --> 00:10:41,840
the court give a harsher sentence?

272
00:10:41,910 --> 00:10:42,970
Yes, I've decided.

273
00:10:43,510 --> 00:10:44,670
The maximum sentence

274
00:10:44,670 --> 00:10:45,770
for hooliganism is
only 7 years of imprisonment.

275
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:47,230
It's too easy on the Wangs.

276
00:10:47,790 --> 00:10:49,630
How long do you think is appropriate?

277
00:10:49,630 --> 00:10:50,360
Ten years.

278
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:53,720
Even if the number goes up to 15,

279
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:55,380
it'll still serve them right.

280
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:05,430
Didn't we agree

281
00:11:05,430 --> 00:11:07,560
not to meet at each other's workplace?

282
00:11:07,790 --> 00:11:09,520
Why? Afraid of people talking?

283
00:11:10,750 --> 00:11:13,080
No, just the inconvenience of coming out.

284
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:15,040
What's up?

285
00:11:15,550 --> 00:11:16,410
You look upset.

286
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:21,370
Bring these to your father.

287
00:11:21,750 --> 00:11:22,510
Didn't we make a pact?

288
00:11:22,510 --> 00:11:23,360
You're supposed to bring them

289
00:11:23,360 --> 00:11:24,100
to tonight's dinner.

290
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:25,900
Why are you giving them to me now?

291
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:27,580
I'll bail on it.

292
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:31,200
Yu Gaoyuan, what are you trying to say?

293
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:32,000
Just spill it.

294
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:35,660
Your father

295
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:38,030
is Fang Leiming, right?

296
00:11:38,030 --> 00:11:39,320
Yes. Is there a problem?

297
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:40,320
He's a regional military commander.

298
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:41,030
A deputy one.

299
00:11:41,030 --> 00:11:41,910
What difference does it make?

300
00:11:41,910 --> 00:11:42,320
Yeah.

301
00:11:42,870 --> 00:11:44,530
What difference does it make?

302
00:11:46,790 --> 00:11:48,090
Does it make

303
00:11:48,130 --> 00:11:48,910
any difference to you

304
00:11:48,910 --> 00:11:49,380
whether he is

305
00:11:49,380 --> 00:11:51,030
a breeder or a military commander?

306
00:11:51,030 --> 00:11:52,830
I didn't mean to hide it from you.

307
00:11:53,390 --> 00:11:55,520
It wouldn't be necessary or possible.

308
00:11:55,740 --> 00:11:56,600
I just wanted us

309
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:57,390
to get off

310
00:11:57,390 --> 00:11:58,440
on a simple start.

311
00:12:01,270 --> 00:12:02,170
If you think I handled it poorly,

312
00:12:02,170 --> 00:12:03,500
then I apologize to you.

313
00:12:03,910 --> 00:12:05,550
So you did have concerns, right?

314
00:12:05,550 --> 00:12:05,950
Right.

315
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:07,600
I did.

316
00:12:09,320 --> 00:12:11,050
I just... I just feared that...

317
00:12:11,550 --> 00:12:13,150
Well, I overthought things.

318
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:14,150
I just doubted

319
00:12:14,150 --> 00:12:15,290
if you approached me

320
00:12:15,320 --> 00:12:16,390
and pretended to like me

321
00:12:16,390 --> 00:12:18,120
because of my father's status.

322
00:12:20,920 --> 00:12:22,360
What? Just because I'm from a rural place,

323
00:12:22,360 --> 00:12:23,890
I'm not good enough for you?

324
00:12:24,870 --> 00:12:25,530
No, it's me.

325
00:12:26,390 --> 00:12:27,980
Because of my leg, I feel inferior

326
00:12:27,980 --> 00:12:29,440
and I'm sensitive and suspicious.

327
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:31,360
It is I who is not good enough for you.
Okay?

328
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:32,870
You're a judge who graduated from

329
00:12:32,870 --> 00:12:35,440
a prestigious university
and you excel in every way.

330
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:37,640
Would you possibly fall in love with me?

331
00:12:42,150 --> 00:12:42,750
Forget it.

332
00:12:44,270 --> 00:12:45,070
You're proud,

333
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:46,850
and I feel inferior.

334
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:48,870
Our relationship was only a coincidence.

335
00:12:48,870 --> 00:12:50,200
I was thinking too much.

336
00:13:19,130 --> 00:13:20,730
Let go. People are watching.

337
00:13:21,120 --> 00:13:22,440
Then let them.

338
00:13:22,670 --> 00:13:23,440
It hurts.

339
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:31,800
It really hurts.
You're pressing on my ear.

340
00:13:38,790 --> 00:13:39,590
Let me ask you.

341
00:13:41,630 --> 00:13:43,490
What exactly do you like about me?

342
00:13:45,320 --> 00:13:45,850
Your leg.

343
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:52,790
Is it because I look like

344
00:13:52,790 --> 00:13:54,720
that girl you went to collage with?

345
00:13:55,390 --> 00:13:56,720
You're not like anyone.

346
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:00,030
Fang Haohao,

347
00:14:00,030 --> 00:14:01,160
I'm 27 years old now.

348
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:04,100
I was in a relationship

349
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:05,910
that failed badly.

350
00:14:05,910 --> 00:14:06,860
I handled some major problems

351
00:14:06,860 --> 00:14:07,860
in a terrible way,

352
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:12,800
and hence lost many friends.

353
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:16,670
Everything I said that day

354
00:14:16,670 --> 00:14:17,790
when I first met you

355
00:14:18,910 --> 00:14:19,440
is true.

356
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:21,120
None of it is a lie.

357
00:14:25,510 --> 00:14:27,310
I like you for no other reason...

358
00:14:28,150 --> 00:14:28,950
than just you.

359
00:14:46,750 --> 00:14:47,680
Take these back.

360
00:14:48,960 --> 00:14:50,220
Don't be late tonight.

361
00:14:59,200 --> 00:14:59,800
This is it.

362
00:15:06,480 --> 00:15:07,010
Oh right.

363
00:15:08,080 --> 00:15:09,140
I have a stepmother

364
00:15:09,550 --> 00:15:11,150
who is not much older than us.

365
00:15:11,590 --> 00:15:12,670
She likes stirring up trouble.

366
00:15:12,670 --> 00:15:13,770
If she acts up later,

367
00:15:13,770 --> 00:15:14,700
just ignore her.

368
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:16,980
Why do you always spring surprises on me?

369
00:15:17,120 --> 00:15:18,630
Saying it sooner or later is all the same.

370
00:15:18,630 --> 00:15:19,510
You're here to meet

371
00:15:19,510 --> 00:15:20,240
my father, not her.

372
00:15:20,240 --> 00:15:20,670
Let's go.

373
00:15:20,670 --> 00:15:22,000
Let me carry that stuff.

374
00:15:22,230 --> 00:15:23,760
Tidy up my clothes, please.

375
00:15:23,790 --> 00:15:24,440
Fix them.

376
00:15:27,670 --> 00:15:28,470
You look fine.

377
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:30,240
I'm a bit nervous.

378
00:15:30,240 --> 00:15:30,770
Let's go.

379
00:15:32,390 --> 00:15:32,960
Carry you on my back?

380
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:33,420
No need.

381
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:34,130
Let's do.

382
00:15:34,150 --> 00:15:34,610
No need.

383
00:15:35,440 --> 00:15:36,240
No need at all!

384
00:15:38,630 --> 00:15:39,550
Come on in now.

385
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:40,840
They're waiting.

386
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:42,000
Welcome home!

387
00:15:42,150 --> 00:15:43,320
Come on. Take a seat in here.

388
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:44,650
Let me take your things.

389
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:46,840
Dad,

390
00:15:47,630 --> 00:15:48,600
this is Yu Gaoyuan.

391
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:50,320
He works at
the Municipal Intermediate People's Court.

392
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:51,250
Hello, Mr. Fang.

393
00:15:53,750 --> 00:15:54,550
Go have a seat.

394
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:03,160
I've heard many good things about you
from Haohao.

395
00:16:03,450 --> 00:16:04,550
She has rarely praised anyone

396
00:16:04,550 --> 00:16:05,810
ever since she's a kid.

397
00:16:06,870 --> 00:16:07,540
Zhang,

398
00:16:07,870 --> 00:16:09,330
bring some slippers over.

399
00:16:10,030 --> 00:16:11,030
No need for those.

400
00:16:11,320 --> 00:16:12,270
My dad tracks mud everywhere

401
00:16:12,270 --> 00:16:14,270
anyway when he finishes gardening.

402
00:16:18,750 --> 00:16:19,280
Mr. Fang,

403
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:20,030
Haohao specifically

404
00:16:20,030 --> 00:16:20,960
told me to buy these.

405
00:16:20,960 --> 00:16:21,550
Previously, I took

406
00:16:21,550 --> 00:16:22,220
a trip to Beijing

407
00:16:22,220 --> 00:16:24,150
and bought these pastries for you.

408
00:16:25,510 --> 00:16:27,240
He can't eat too much of these,

409
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:29,730
due to his high blood sugar.

410
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:31,240
Zhang!

411
00:16:31,630 --> 00:16:32,200
Coming!

412
00:16:32,670 --> 00:16:33,070
Hurry.

413
00:16:36,150 --> 00:16:37,610
What a handsome young man.

414
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:39,720
It's a blessing for Haohao

415
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:42,100
that you are attracted to her.

416
00:16:43,910 --> 00:16:45,120
It's also a blessing for you.

417
00:16:45,120 --> 00:16:45,890
Pressure, too.

418
00:16:45,890 --> 00:16:46,220
Yes.

419
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:47,720
Haohao

420
00:16:47,750 --> 00:16:49,000
is no ordinary girl.

421
00:16:49,240 --> 00:16:50,270
You have to tame her,

422
00:16:50,270 --> 00:16:51,270
or you'll suffer.

423
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:56,010
Am I right, Fang?

424
00:17:02,440 --> 00:17:03,240
Eat some more.

425
00:17:05,589 --> 00:17:06,349
Haohao...

426
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:08,250
has been good at poetry,

427
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:11,240
calligraphy, and painting

428
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:12,250
since she was this tall.

429
00:17:12,250 --> 00:17:14,000
She always got the first place
in speech contests,

430
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:14,750
math contests,

431
00:17:14,750 --> 00:17:16,310
language competitions, and whatsoever.

432
00:17:16,310 --> 00:17:17,680
She excels in everything!

433
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:19,140
Isn't that right, Haohao?

434
00:17:22,400 --> 00:17:24,460
It's a pity that she has a permanently

435
00:17:24,589 --> 00:17:25,319
damaged leg.

436
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:27,560
What a shame.

437
00:17:27,589 --> 00:17:29,160
God must be jealous of her.

438
00:17:29,310 --> 00:17:31,000
God has no mercy.

439
00:17:31,710 --> 00:17:32,750
Mr. Fang, easy on the drinks.

440
00:17:32,750 --> 00:17:33,880
Have some more food.

441
00:17:34,030 --> 00:17:35,270
Just call me Fang!

442
00:17:35,830 --> 00:17:37,450
Why put a "mister" before it?

443
00:17:38,120 --> 00:17:40,250
You'll be calling me Dad in the future.

444
00:17:40,830 --> 00:17:41,890
He's right.

445
00:17:42,030 --> 00:17:43,090
Easy on the drinks.

446
00:17:43,830 --> 00:17:44,400
What now?

447
00:17:44,830 --> 00:17:46,430
Are you looking for trouble?

448
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:48,700
Go get me the pastries.

449
00:17:48,880 --> 00:17:50,310
My daughter had them bought for me.

450
00:17:50,310 --> 00:17:51,510
I want to eat them now!

451
00:17:58,640 --> 00:18:00,110
Haohao got in this condition

452
00:18:00,110 --> 00:18:01,770
when she was in kindergarten.

453
00:18:03,110 --> 00:18:04,840
Her real mom passed away early.

454
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:06,880
She suffered this because of me.

455
00:18:08,110 --> 00:18:09,170
It was all my fault!

456
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:10,980
You did nothing wrong.

457
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:14,020
I just had bad luck.

458
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:16,720
How stubborn.

459
00:18:16,920 --> 00:18:18,520
She takes that after her mom.

460
00:18:19,110 --> 00:18:21,440
Haohao has a sharp tongue
but a soft heart.

461
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:23,080
She specifically asked me

462
00:18:23,080 --> 00:18:23,920
to buy those pastries for you

463
00:18:23,920 --> 00:18:25,840
from Daoxiangcun's head store
on Dongsi Street.

464
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:26,680
She even made a list

465
00:18:26,680 --> 00:18:27,510
of what you enjoy

466
00:18:27,510 --> 00:18:28,200
eating.

467
00:18:28,700 --> 00:18:29,400
I almost missed

468
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:30,460
the train for that.

469
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:34,160
Yu.

470
00:18:35,810 --> 00:18:36,870
I've seen plenty of

471
00:18:36,880 --> 00:18:37,940
young men like you.

472
00:18:39,770 --> 00:18:42,130
Having humble origins. Calculating.

473
00:18:42,160 --> 00:18:44,480
Smart. Aiming high.

474
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:46,210
Puffed with ambitions,

475
00:18:46,240 --> 00:18:47,440
and very realistic.

476
00:18:49,310 --> 00:18:50,570
But it doesn't matter!

477
00:18:51,250 --> 00:18:51,920
You managed to quickly

478
00:18:51,920 --> 00:18:53,000
win my daughter's heart over.

479
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,200
That was no easy feat.

480
00:18:54,550 --> 00:18:56,750
You're quite an outstanding young lad.

481
00:18:57,200 --> 00:18:57,800
That said,

482
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:01,960
I don't care about your motives,

483
00:19:02,740 --> 00:19:03,760
or if you truly

484
00:19:03,790 --> 00:19:04,790
love my daughter.

485
00:19:05,830 --> 00:19:07,490
Just you remember, young lad,

486
00:19:08,240 --> 00:19:09,700
to treat my daughter well,

487
00:19:09,830 --> 00:19:11,480
even if you have to fake it.

488
00:19:12,130 --> 00:19:13,130
Otherwise, I will

489
00:19:13,160 --> 00:19:14,360
hunt you down one day.

490
00:19:16,350 --> 00:19:17,210
Did you hear me?

491
00:19:19,110 --> 00:19:19,770
I heard you.

492
00:19:21,170 --> 00:19:22,350
I'll give it my all to make her

493
00:19:22,350 --> 00:19:22,880
happy.

494
00:19:28,220 --> 00:19:28,960
Eat, Mr. Fang.

495
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:30,260
Sure. Sure.

496
00:19:38,640 --> 00:19:39,160
You'd hate

497
00:19:39,160 --> 00:19:40,890
to come to my home again, right?

498
00:19:41,590 --> 00:19:42,990
Not just you, even I don't

499
00:19:43,790 --> 00:19:45,250
want to be back here again.

500
00:19:46,720 --> 00:19:47,920
Your father really loves you.

501
00:19:47,920 --> 00:19:50,250
It's understandable that he lectured me.

502
00:19:50,510 --> 00:19:52,110
He didn't do that out of love.

503
00:19:52,360 --> 00:19:53,070
He just couldn't wait

504
00:19:53,070 --> 00:19:53,900
to get rid of me.

505
00:19:53,900 --> 00:19:55,760
Then his life will be much easier.

506
00:19:58,920 --> 00:20:00,680
It's always been like this
since I was little.

507
00:20:00,680 --> 00:20:01,880
I've grown used to it.

508
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:02,910
In this world,

509
00:20:03,200 --> 00:20:04,860
one can still live well alone.

510
00:20:05,550 --> 00:20:06,610
I don't need a home,

511
00:20:06,790 --> 00:20:08,590
nor do I expect anyone to love me.

512
00:20:11,880 --> 00:20:13,280
Alright, don't be upset.

513
00:20:13,720 --> 00:20:15,180
Let's change the subject.

514
00:20:17,270 --> 00:20:18,640
When I get off work tomorrow,

515
00:20:18,640 --> 00:20:19,440
let's meet up.

516
00:20:20,790 --> 00:20:21,160
Why?

517
00:20:22,440 --> 00:20:24,170
I'd like you to meet my parents.

518
00:20:25,110 --> 00:20:25,830
It's unnecessary.

519
00:20:25,830 --> 00:20:27,160
How so? It is necessary.

520
00:20:30,070 --> 00:20:31,240
I don't need your pity.

521
00:20:31,240 --> 00:20:33,240
Who's pitying you? I'm begging you.

522
00:20:33,750 --> 00:20:34,880
Begging me for what?

523
00:20:40,590 --> 00:20:42,200
For your hand in marriage.

524
00:20:51,070 --> 00:20:52,200
What's in it for you?

525
00:20:53,170 --> 00:20:53,960
What's in it for me?

526
00:20:53,960 --> 00:20:55,160
Let me think about it.

527
00:20:57,720 --> 00:20:58,680
I aim to marry up,

528
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:01,440
to suck up to Commander Fang,

529
00:21:01,640 --> 00:21:03,500
and to score a successful career.

530
00:21:04,550 --> 00:21:05,350
You happy now?

531
00:21:15,350 --> 00:21:16,410
It's settled then.

532
00:21:24,720 --> 00:21:26,360
Let's meet my parents tomorrow

533
00:21:26,360 --> 00:21:27,820
and get married on Monday.

534
00:21:57,590 --> 00:21:58,320
You're back.

535
00:21:59,030 --> 00:22:00,430
Why are you still up, Dad?

536
00:22:01,120 --> 00:22:02,640
With things on my mind,

537
00:22:03,820 --> 00:22:04,950
how can I fall sleep?

538
00:22:05,480 --> 00:22:06,610
What's on your mind?

539
00:22:12,030 --> 00:22:13,400
Only when I saw with my own eyes

540
00:22:13,400 --> 00:22:15,070
your abode in Binjiang

541
00:22:15,790 --> 00:22:17,120
and the clothes you wear

542
00:22:18,090 --> 00:22:19,160
did I finally believe

543
00:22:19,160 --> 00:22:20,480
that my son really grew up

544
00:22:20,480 --> 00:22:21,810
and became an official.

545
00:22:23,790 --> 00:22:25,120
I'm not an official yet.

546
00:22:27,550 --> 00:22:28,480
How are my brother and sister

547
00:22:28,480 --> 00:22:29,280
doing at home?

548
00:22:30,440 --> 00:22:31,570
They're doing fine.

549
00:22:33,400 --> 00:22:35,600
When I get better off in a few more years,

550
00:22:36,510 --> 00:22:38,040
I'll have you all move here.

551
00:22:42,200 --> 00:22:44,480
The year you took
the college entrance exam,

552
00:22:44,480 --> 00:22:46,940
I burned joss paper
at the ancestral graves,

553
00:22:46,960 --> 00:22:48,360
praying to our ancestors

554
00:22:48,590 --> 00:22:51,050
for helping a descendant of ours
to succeed.

555
00:22:51,550 --> 00:22:52,880
Who would have thought?

556
00:22:53,310 --> 00:22:55,110
After graduating from college,

557
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:57,360
my son was assigned to this little town.

558
00:22:58,030 --> 00:22:59,240
At the thought of you

559
00:22:59,480 --> 00:23:00,680
getting married here

560
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:01,510
and probably being tied down

561
00:23:01,510 --> 00:23:03,200
right here for the test of your life,

562
00:23:03,200 --> 00:23:05,070
I'm upset.

563
00:23:10,960 --> 00:23:13,020
When we eat, we take one bite at a time.

564
00:23:13,590 --> 00:23:15,720
When we walk, we take one step at a time.

565
00:23:19,830 --> 00:23:20,760
Go to sleep, Dad.

566
00:23:21,750 --> 00:23:22,790
Time to tuck in.

567
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:49,810
The inmates here

568
00:23:50,030 --> 00:23:51,790
are all felons, most of which

569
00:23:52,070 --> 00:23:54,460
are on death row with reprieve
or life imprisonment.

570
00:23:54,460 --> 00:23:55,640
When a prisoner is transferred here,

571
00:23:55,640 --> 00:23:57,830
his original household registration
will be revoked

572
00:23:57,830 --> 00:23:59,240
and moved to Bieshan, namely here.

573
00:23:59,240 --> 00:23:59,880
This causes

574
00:23:59,880 --> 00:24:01,680
strong resistance among the inmates

575
00:24:01,680 --> 00:24:02,790
and increases the difficulty

576
00:24:02,790 --> 00:24:03,650
of management.

577
00:24:06,110 --> 00:24:06,680
Guys,

578
00:24:06,750 --> 00:24:07,880
there's a girl here!

579
00:24:11,350 --> 00:24:12,350
The more you fear,

580
00:24:12,750 --> 00:24:13,640
the more they enjoy it.

581
00:24:13,640 --> 00:24:15,550
-Hey, girl!
-Hey, lady!

582
00:24:16,510 --> 00:24:17,030
Hey, girl!

583
00:24:17,030 --> 00:24:17,630
Look here!

584
00:24:19,270 --> 00:24:19,930
Young lady!

585
00:24:21,200 --> 00:24:22,130
Girl, look at me!

586
00:24:23,030 --> 00:24:23,630
Hey, girl.

587
00:24:24,510 --> 00:24:26,110
You have a really slim waist.

588
00:24:27,590 --> 00:24:28,390
Song Changhe,

589
00:24:28,890 --> 00:24:30,200
do you want to throw away the points

590
00:24:30,200 --> 00:24:31,510
you've collected this month?

591
00:24:31,510 --> 00:24:33,240
Don't do that, Prosecutor Guo.

592
00:24:33,440 --> 00:24:34,950
W-We're just giving her

593
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:35,880
a warm welcome, aren't we?

594
00:24:35,880 --> 00:24:37,080
-Welcome!
-Welcome!

595
00:24:39,110 --> 00:24:40,910
Apologize to Prosecutor Zhang!

596
00:24:42,640 --> 00:24:43,700
Look at him, so mad.

597
00:24:44,590 --> 00:24:45,650
Prosecutor Zhang,

598
00:24:46,160 --> 00:24:47,480
my apologies.

599
00:24:51,720 --> 00:24:54,350
-She's coming over!
-She is!

600
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:56,760
You're Song Changhe, right?

601
00:24:57,750 --> 00:24:59,010
You had better behave.

602
00:24:59,350 --> 00:25:00,410
I'll remember you.

603
00:25:00,960 --> 00:25:02,160
She'll remember you!

604
00:25:02,290 --> 00:25:05,130
-She said she'd remember you!
-Listen to that!

605
00:25:05,160 --> 00:25:05,960
My apologies,

606
00:25:06,510 --> 00:25:07,240
Prosecutor Zhang.

607
00:25:07,240 --> 00:25:07,830
Speak up!

608
00:25:08,070 --> 00:25:09,000
I can't hear you!

609
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:11,240
-She's feisty.
-So tough.

610
00:25:11,240 --> 00:25:12,040
My apologies,

611
00:25:12,070 --> 00:25:13,130
Prosecutor Zhang!

612
00:25:13,510 --> 00:25:14,640
You just caved like that?

613
00:25:14,640 --> 00:25:15,170
He caved!

614
00:25:17,750 --> 00:25:19,030
You chicken!

615
00:25:21,400 --> 00:25:21,960
Now,

616
00:25:22,240 --> 00:25:23,370
the prosecutor will

617
00:25:23,680 --> 00:25:24,880
read the indictment.

618
00:25:29,310 --> 00:25:31,310
Honorable Presiding Judge, Judge,

619
00:25:31,960 --> 00:25:33,400
and People's Assessors,

620
00:25:33,790 --> 00:25:34,270
now,

621
00:25:34,640 --> 00:25:36,240
appointed by and on behalf

622
00:25:36,440 --> 00:25:37,900
of the Binjiang Municipal

623
00:25:38,070 --> 00:25:40,640
People's Procuratorate,

624
00:25:41,200 --> 00:25:42,790
I am initiating a public prosecution

625
00:25:42,790 --> 00:25:43,830
against a hooligan gang

626
00:25:43,830 --> 00:25:45,440
of four, including Wang Youxi

627
00:25:45,440 --> 00:25:46,440
and Liang Yuemin.

628
00:25:47,070 --> 00:25:49,600
The trial will proceed
under my supervision.

629
00:25:52,920 --> 00:25:54,750
You said you didn't commit the murder.

630
00:25:54,750 --> 00:25:55,350
Any proof?

631
00:25:55,920 --> 00:25:56,960
I didn't kill,

632
00:25:57,410 --> 00:25:58,550
and I have to provide proof of it?

633
00:25:58,550 --> 00:25:59,310
Of course.

634
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:01,640
The procuratorate has plenty of evidence

635
00:26:01,640 --> 00:26:02,840
to prove you did the murder.

636
00:26:02,840 --> 00:26:04,210
They are holding

637
00:26:04,240 --> 00:26:05,590
all the trump cards.

638
00:26:05,790 --> 00:26:06,830
What do you have?

639
00:26:08,480 --> 00:26:09,160
Besides,

640
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:11,960
only now are you saying you didn't kill.

641
00:26:11,960 --> 00:26:13,440
W-Why did you admit guilt earlier?

642
00:26:13,440 --> 00:26:14,030
Because they...

643
00:26:14,030 --> 00:26:14,750
Cut it out.

644
00:26:15,500 --> 00:26:15,980
Listen,

645
00:26:16,400 --> 00:26:17,260
take my advice.

646
00:26:17,440 --> 00:26:18,300
Don't fight it.

647
00:26:18,790 --> 00:26:19,880
Prioritize your life.

648
00:26:19,880 --> 00:26:21,080
When you get to court,

649
00:26:21,350 --> 00:26:23,040
actively plead guilty, show remorse,

650
00:26:23,040 --> 00:26:24,110
and beg for a lenient sentence.

651
00:26:24,110 --> 00:26:25,570
Don't irritate the judge.

652
00:26:25,740 --> 00:26:27,590
Strive for a death sentence with reprieve.

653
00:26:27,590 --> 00:26:29,310
There will be
a trial of second instance, right?

654
00:26:29,310 --> 00:26:30,640
Try to claim your innocence then.

655
00:26:30,640 --> 00:26:31,270
As for me,

656
00:26:32,460 --> 00:26:33,400
I'll collect more evidence

657
00:26:33,400 --> 00:26:34,410
to your advantage.

658
00:26:34,410 --> 00:26:35,830
What if I'm really sentenced to death?

659
00:26:35,830 --> 00:26:37,230
What do you think I can do?

660
00:26:39,350 --> 00:26:40,950
You might as well fire me now.

661
00:26:46,960 --> 00:26:47,760
Their actions

662
00:26:48,480 --> 00:26:51,210
not only inflicted severe trauma
on the victims,

663
00:26:51,960 --> 00:26:53,090
but also undermined

664
00:26:53,350 --> 00:26:54,950
the national law, humanity,

665
00:26:55,110 --> 00:26:55,970
and moraliity.

666
00:26:56,880 --> 00:26:58,070
I, as the prosecutor,

667
00:26:58,070 --> 00:26:59,800
hereby specifically point out

668
00:27:00,160 --> 00:27:01,480
that the defendants in this case

669
00:27:01,480 --> 00:27:03,570
have shown no recognition
of their crimes to date

670
00:27:03,570 --> 00:27:04,500
and have refused

671
00:27:04,680 --> 00:27:05,880
to admit their guilt.

672
00:27:06,310 --> 00:27:07,410
The defendants' behavior

673
00:27:07,410 --> 00:27:08,670
is a blatant challenge

674
00:27:08,680 --> 00:27:09,880
to the fundamental bounds

675
00:27:09,880 --> 00:27:11,140
of the law and morality

676
00:27:11,480 --> 00:27:12,810
honored by our society.

677
00:27:13,160 --> 00:27:14,440
They must be severely punished.

678
00:27:14,440 --> 00:27:15,100
Therefore,

679
00:27:15,920 --> 00:27:17,920
the prosecution strongly suggests

680
00:27:18,110 --> 00:27:20,270
that in accordance to
Article 1 of the Decision

681
00:27:20,270 --> 00:27:21,530
on Severely Punishing

682
00:27:21,560 --> 00:27:23,070
the Criminals Constituting

683
00:27:23,070 --> 00:27:23,800
Grave Damage

684
00:27:23,830 --> 00:27:27,110
on Public Security, which was approved
by the standing committed

685
00:27:27,110 --> 00:27:28,400
of the National People's Congress

686
00:27:28,400 --> 00:27:29,640
on September 2, 1983,

687
00:27:30,200 --> 00:27:32,070
the defendants in this case should be

688
00:27:32,070 --> 00:27:34,800
sentenced above
the statutory maximum penalty.

689
00:27:36,270 --> 00:27:37,550
Harsh punishments will serve them right!

690
00:27:37,550 --> 00:27:37,950
Bravo!

691
00:27:38,090 --> 00:27:39,160
-Well said!
-Bravo!

692
00:27:39,160 --> 00:27:40,240
They deserve severe sentences!

693
00:27:40,240 --> 00:27:42,240
What were they thinking
when they beat others up?

694
00:27:42,240 --> 00:27:42,640
Bravo!

695
00:27:46,880 --> 00:27:48,070
Order in the court!

696
00:27:49,720 --> 00:27:50,830
Order in the court!

697
00:27:53,160 --> 00:27:54,820
The hearing is now concluded.

698
00:27:55,240 --> 00:27:57,260
Sentencing will be announced
at a later date.

699
00:27:57,260 --> 00:27:58,040
Adjourned!

700
00:28:08,590 --> 00:28:09,050
Mentor!

701
00:28:11,510 --> 00:28:12,440
Anything wrong?

702
00:28:13,320 --> 00:28:13,830
We discussed

703
00:28:13,830 --> 00:28:14,420
the submission

704
00:28:14,420 --> 00:28:15,350
for sentencing.

705
00:28:15,680 --> 00:28:16,740
You agreed with it.

706
00:28:17,030 --> 00:28:18,360
Right, I did say the case

707
00:28:18,640 --> 00:28:19,970
would be yours to handle

708
00:28:20,070 --> 00:28:20,730
and decide.

709
00:28:21,110 --> 00:28:22,570
Then why are you like this?

710
00:28:22,640 --> 00:28:23,450
Are you regretting it?

711
00:28:23,450 --> 00:28:24,170
Do you know

712
00:28:24,200 --> 00:28:25,130
that what you just said

713
00:28:25,130 --> 00:28:25,960
will stir up public hostility

714
00:28:25,960 --> 00:28:27,310
towards the defendants?

715
00:28:27,310 --> 00:28:28,910
But everything I said is true.

716
00:28:28,910 --> 00:28:29,510
Is that so?

717
00:28:29,680 --> 00:28:29,940
Yes.

718
00:28:29,940 --> 00:28:31,670
Do you really think it that way?

719
00:28:41,550 --> 00:28:42,110
Mr. Tan.

720
00:28:42,960 --> 00:28:43,410
Hello.

721
00:28:43,450 --> 00:28:44,070
My surname is Xia.

722
00:28:44,070 --> 00:28:44,700
I'm the associate judge

723
00:28:44,700 --> 00:28:45,500
for this case.

724
00:28:45,550 --> 00:28:46,320
Nice to meet you.

725
00:28:46,320 --> 00:28:47,680
I'm here to submit
the representation papers

726
00:28:47,680 --> 00:28:49,210
and the defense statement.

727
00:28:59,200 --> 00:29:01,060
So this is the defense statement?

728
00:29:01,720 --> 00:29:02,650
Anything wrong?

729
00:29:02,920 --> 00:29:03,590
The defendant

730
00:29:03,590 --> 00:29:04,220
in this case might be

731
00:29:04,220 --> 00:29:05,480
given a death sentence.

732
00:29:05,480 --> 00:29:06,650
Please don't worry.

733
00:29:06,680 --> 00:29:08,080
I've educated my client.

734
00:29:08,210 --> 00:29:08,790
He will refrain

735
00:29:08,790 --> 00:29:10,160
from talking nonsense in court,

736
00:29:10,160 --> 00:29:11,730
actively admit his guilt,
receive punishment,

737
00:29:11,730 --> 00:29:12,240
and sincerely

738
00:29:12,240 --> 00:29:14,030
apologize to the victim's family,

739
00:29:14,030 --> 00:29:16,160
so as to strive for a lighter sentence.

740
00:29:18,760 --> 00:29:19,720
How are you going to fight

741
00:29:19,720 --> 00:29:21,450
for a lighter sentence for him?

742
00:29:22,010 --> 00:29:23,830
The defendant had a conflict
with the victim

743
00:29:23,830 --> 00:29:25,270
due to family issues.

744
00:29:26,090 --> 00:29:26,640
They should have

745
00:29:26,640 --> 00:29:28,160
resolved the problems properly

746
00:29:28,160 --> 00:29:30,080
through consultation,
guided by correct values.

747
00:29:30,080 --> 00:29:30,790
However, the defendant

748
00:29:30,790 --> 00:29:33,000
failed to properly settle family disputes.

749
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:34,400
Harboring evil intents,

750
00:29:34,590 --> 00:29:36,720
he killed and dismembered the victim,

751
00:29:37,310 --> 00:29:39,910
displaying utterly grave
subjective malice.

752
00:29:40,310 --> 00:29:42,030
The defendant employed
exceptionally cruel means.

753
00:29:42,030 --> 00:29:44,310
The circumstances of his offense
were especially egregious,

754
00:29:44,310 --> 00:29:47,240
resulting in
extraordinarily grave social impact.

755
00:29:48,070 --> 00:29:48,960
The defendant in this case

756
00:29:48,960 --> 00:29:50,110
deprived another of life

757
00:29:50,110 --> 00:29:52,440
and dismembered the body with cruel means.

758
00:29:52,440 --> 00:29:53,100
His actions

759
00:29:53,200 --> 00:29:55,830
constitute the crime
of intentional homicide.

760
00:29:55,830 --> 00:29:57,110
He merits

761
00:29:57,240 --> 00:29:58,770
the maximum penalty of law.

762
00:29:59,240 --> 00:29:59,900
Defendant,

763
00:30:00,550 --> 00:30:01,880
do you plead guilty to the crimes

764
00:30:01,880 --> 00:30:03,010
you are charged with

765
00:30:03,130 --> 00:30:04,190
in the indictment?

766
00:30:04,590 --> 00:30:05,390
I am innocent.

767
00:30:05,520 --> 00:30:07,200
Presiding Judge, I really am innocent!

768
00:30:07,200 --> 00:30:08,640
I didn't kill her.

769
00:30:09,790 --> 00:30:10,160
Okay.

770
00:30:10,680 --> 00:30:12,340
The court notes your opinion.

771
00:30:13,030 --> 00:30:13,630
Defender,

772
00:30:14,510 --> 00:30:15,720
what is your defense?

773
00:30:18,270 --> 00:30:19,880
The indictment consists of

774
00:30:20,030 --> 00:30:21,310
clear facts of the crimes

775
00:30:21,310 --> 00:30:22,770
and conclusive evidence.

776
00:30:22,920 --> 00:30:25,120
I, as the defender, have no objections.

777
00:30:25,350 --> 00:30:27,440
However, the defense
would like to point out

778
00:30:27,440 --> 00:30:28,550
that the killing in this case

779
00:30:28,550 --> 00:30:30,110
happened in the heat of passion

780
00:30:30,110 --> 00:30:32,350
triggered by escalated family conflicts.

781
00:30:32,350 --> 00:30:34,200
So its danger to the society
is relatively small.

782
00:30:34,200 --> 00:30:35,880
Regarding the cause of the incident,

783
00:30:35,880 --> 00:30:36,750
it cannot be said

784
00:30:36,750 --> 00:30:38,950
the victim was entirely without fault.

785
00:30:39,030 --> 00:30:40,230
As a wife, she allowed

786
00:30:40,400 --> 00:30:42,030
a third party to intrude
into her marriage,

787
00:30:42,030 --> 00:30:43,550
pressured the defendant for a divorce,

788
00:30:43,550 --> 00:30:45,280
and refused to return to the defendant

789
00:30:45,280 --> 00:30:46,110
the bride price he paid

790
00:30:46,110 --> 00:30:47,110
to marry her,

791
00:30:47,510 --> 00:30:48,720
hence causing constant tension

792
00:30:48,720 --> 00:30:49,960
in their relationship.

793
00:30:49,960 --> 00:30:50,920
For that, the defendant

794
00:30:50,920 --> 00:30:52,520
fell into a state of despair.

795
00:30:52,960 --> 00:30:55,110
The defendant always behaved well

796
00:30:55,440 --> 00:30:56,440
and abided by the law.

797
00:30:56,440 --> 00:30:58,960
This is his first offense
and an isolated incident.

798
00:30:58,960 --> 00:31:01,400
After his arrest,
he truthfully confessed to his crimes

799
00:31:01,400 --> 00:31:03,030
with a cooperative attitude.

800
00:31:03,030 --> 00:31:03,690
Therefore,

801
00:31:04,440 --> 00:31:05,640
the defense believes

802
00:31:05,920 --> 00:31:07,350
that the defendant should be

803
00:31:07,350 --> 00:31:08,810
given a lighter sentence.

804
00:31:09,310 --> 00:31:10,370
I deny the charges!

805
00:31:11,000 --> 00:31:12,350
I didn't kill my wife!

806
00:31:13,160 --> 00:31:14,510
Don't you gang up

807
00:31:14,510 --> 00:31:16,050
to frame me.

808
00:31:18,110 --> 00:31:19,580
And you said the defendant admitted guilt

809
00:31:19,580 --> 00:31:21,000
with a cooperative attitude?

810
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:23,590
I really am innocent!

811
00:31:24,070 --> 00:31:26,200
Why don't you believe me?

812
00:31:27,240 --> 00:31:28,500
Defendant, calm down.

813
00:31:28,830 --> 00:31:29,630
Let me ask you.

814
00:31:30,270 --> 00:31:31,830
When was the first time

815
00:31:32,110 --> 00:31:33,240
you admitted guilt?

816
00:31:34,030 --> 00:31:35,160
I can't recall.

817
00:31:36,960 --> 00:31:37,620
They told me

818
00:31:38,510 --> 00:31:39,570
they'd let me sleep

819
00:31:40,200 --> 00:31:41,600
as long as I owned up to it.

820
00:31:42,030 --> 00:31:43,830
They made me stay awake for days.

821
00:31:44,530 --> 00:31:45,640
Why did you refuse to admit guilt

822
00:31:45,640 --> 00:31:46,790
in several prior interviews?

823
00:31:46,790 --> 00:31:47,270
Xia,

824
00:31:47,750 --> 00:31:48,840
why did you ask that?

825
00:31:48,840 --> 00:31:50,000
I didn't kill my wife.

826
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:51,660
What guilt was there to admit?

827
00:31:52,030 --> 00:31:53,490
What was there to confess?

828
00:31:53,920 --> 00:31:55,880
I didn't know a thing!

829
00:31:59,480 --> 00:32:01,270
There are five confessions here.

830
00:32:01,270 --> 00:32:02,800
They were all stated by you.

831
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:03,920
In each of them, the time,

832
00:32:03,920 --> 00:32:04,520
the place,

833
00:32:04,590 --> 00:32:05,350
the murder weapon,

834
00:32:05,350 --> 00:32:06,930
and the killing method
are different.

835
00:32:06,930 --> 00:32:07,480
Why?

836
00:32:07,750 --> 00:32:09,680
They instructed me to say all that.

837
00:32:12,270 --> 00:32:13,930
You keep referring to "they."

838
00:32:14,480 --> 00:32:15,240
Who do you mean?

839
00:32:15,240 --> 00:32:15,830
Xia.

840
00:32:16,350 --> 00:32:17,350
Defense counsel,

841
00:32:17,480 --> 00:32:18,680
any response

842
00:32:18,960 --> 00:32:20,360
to the questions I asked?

843
00:32:20,760 --> 00:32:22,290
Do you have anything to say?

844
00:32:25,110 --> 00:32:25,660
No.

845
00:32:38,830 --> 00:32:39,560
Xia Yingjie,

846
00:32:40,030 --> 00:32:41,890
what on earth did you mean by that?

847
00:32:42,280 --> 00:32:42,690
Mei,

848
00:32:42,720 --> 00:32:44,110
as the trial proceeds, I'm finding

849
00:32:44,110 --> 00:32:45,310
more and more doubts.

850
00:32:47,350 --> 00:32:49,250
I still suggest we return the file and ask

851
00:32:49,250 --> 00:32:50,110
the procuratorate to investigate again.

852
00:32:50,110 --> 00:32:51,710
Didn't we have an agreement?

853
00:32:52,110 --> 00:32:54,510
Why are you asking
to return the file again?

854
00:32:58,550 --> 00:33:00,280
Do you think you are being fair?

855
00:33:00,590 --> 00:33:01,830
Just now, in the court,

856
00:33:01,830 --> 00:33:03,880
you were clearly steering
the defense counsel.

857
00:33:03,880 --> 00:33:05,210
You are totally biased!

858
00:33:07,270 --> 00:33:07,640
Fine.

859
00:33:08,070 --> 00:33:08,760
I admit

860
00:33:09,160 --> 00:33:09,690
it's true

861
00:33:10,130 --> 00:33:11,640
that some interview records
provided by the police

862
00:33:11,640 --> 00:33:12,640
lack compliance.

863
00:33:12,930 --> 00:33:13,440
But this is

864
00:33:13,440 --> 00:33:15,360
a sensational case in the whole city.

865
00:33:15,360 --> 00:33:16,070
How can the basic facts

866
00:33:16,070 --> 00:33:17,270
be denied for just a few records

867
00:33:17,270 --> 00:33:19,070
that fail to meet the standards?

868
00:33:19,240 --> 00:33:20,590
One of the basic facts is

869
00:33:20,840 --> 00:33:22,170
that we cannot confirm

870
00:33:22,200 --> 00:33:23,420
the deceased was Yu Sanhua,

871
00:33:23,420 --> 00:33:24,740
Qian Xingliang's wife.

872
00:33:24,740 --> 00:33:26,160
So you firmly believe Qian Xingliang

873
00:33:26,160 --> 00:33:27,440
is not the murderer, right?

874
00:33:27,440 --> 00:33:29,000
Then when you get out later, just announce

875
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:30,970
that he is innocent and is free to walk!

876
00:33:30,970 --> 00:33:31,680
He might or might not be

877
00:33:31,680 --> 00:33:32,720
the murderer.

878
00:33:33,120 --> 00:33:34,480
That's why I only suggested
we return the file

879
00:33:34,480 --> 00:33:35,750
for supplementary investigation.

880
00:33:35,750 --> 00:33:37,080
Keep rationalizing it!

881
00:34:05,830 --> 00:34:06,440
Xia.

882
00:34:08,280 --> 00:34:09,030
I'm sorry.

883
00:34:10,440 --> 00:34:11,280
I might have been

884
00:34:11,280 --> 00:34:12,880
a little emotional just now.

885
00:34:16,880 --> 00:34:17,360
Mei.

886
00:34:20,510 --> 00:34:22,360
I understand every word you said.

887
00:34:22,360 --> 00:34:23,880
You understand all that.

888
00:34:24,679 --> 00:34:25,400
Then why do you

889
00:34:25,400 --> 00:34:27,130
still have to be this stubborn?

890
00:34:27,710 --> 00:34:29,840
Because I don't want blood on my hands.

891
00:34:35,480 --> 00:34:37,139
And is there blood on my hands?

892
00:34:38,800 --> 00:34:39,320
Xia,

893
00:34:40,550 --> 00:34:41,480
could you relent

894
00:34:42,070 --> 00:34:43,530
just this once for my sake?

895
00:34:45,230 --> 00:34:45,840
Mei,

896
00:34:47,480 --> 00:34:49,280
this has nothing to do with that.

897
00:34:49,510 --> 00:34:52,000
The matter is not between us.

898
00:35:07,630 --> 00:35:08,230
Fine then.

899
00:35:10,070 --> 00:35:11,200
The collegial panel

900
00:35:12,280 --> 00:35:13,940
failed to reach a consensus.

901
00:35:15,840 --> 00:35:16,760
Let's report it

902
00:35:18,400 --> 00:35:20,200
to the Adjudication Committee.

903
00:35:26,510 --> 00:35:28,710
Three, two, one.

904
00:35:31,740 --> 00:35:32,430
Fix yourselves up

905
00:35:32,430 --> 00:35:33,440
before we take another photo.

906
00:35:33,440 --> 00:35:33,770
Okay.

907
00:35:34,630 --> 00:35:35,160
Gaoyuan.

908
00:35:36,400 --> 00:35:37,800
Put on your uniform for a photo.

909
00:35:37,800 --> 00:35:39,060
No, I'm not wearing it.

910
00:35:39,630 --> 00:35:41,560
You already brought it. Why say no?

911
00:35:42,760 --> 00:35:43,360
Put it on.

912
00:35:45,070 --> 00:35:45,440
Fine.

913
00:35:45,440 --> 00:35:46,590
I'll take a picture with you two.

914
00:35:46,590 --> 00:35:47,790
Haohao, have a break.

915
00:35:47,860 --> 00:35:48,710
I'll take a photo with them.

916
00:35:48,710 --> 00:35:49,040
Okay.

917
00:35:49,840 --> 00:35:51,760
The three of you take a family photo.

918
00:35:51,760 --> 00:35:52,820
I'll stay out of it.

919
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:00,510
Haohao.

920
00:36:02,010 --> 00:36:03,370
Our family is poor.

921
00:36:03,400 --> 00:36:04,930
We don't have much to offer.

922
00:36:06,000 --> 00:36:07,710
When I married into the family,

923
00:36:07,710 --> 00:36:09,040
Gaoyuan's grandmother

924
00:36:09,070 --> 00:36:10,200
gave this ring to me.

925
00:36:10,400 --> 00:36:11,110
Now, it can

926
00:36:11,440 --> 00:36:12,770
finally be passed down.

927
00:36:13,360 --> 00:36:13,880
Take it.

928
00:36:14,130 --> 00:36:15,450
No, you should keep it.

929
00:36:16,360 --> 00:36:17,800
Customs are changing now.

930
00:36:17,800 --> 00:36:18,710
This is not a tradition anymore.

931
00:36:18,710 --> 00:36:20,000
Just keep it, Auntie.

932
00:36:21,440 --> 00:36:22,840
Still calling me Auntie?

933
00:36:23,230 --> 00:36:25,190
You won't call me Mom
until after the wedding.

934
00:36:25,190 --> 00:36:25,800
Right?

935
00:36:26,480 --> 00:36:28,210
No need for any changes, Mom.

936
00:36:28,920 --> 00:36:30,810
Haohao isn't used to calling anyone Mom.

937
00:36:30,810 --> 00:36:32,410
Just let her call you Auntie.

938
00:36:34,760 --> 00:36:35,560
So this is what

939
00:36:36,440 --> 00:36:38,770
a high-ranking official's child is like.

940
00:36:39,010 --> 00:36:40,150
You declined the ring

941
00:36:40,150 --> 00:36:41,230
or to call me Mom.

942
00:36:42,880 --> 00:36:43,280
Mom.

943
00:36:45,150 --> 00:36:46,210
I'll take the ring.

944
00:36:46,280 --> 00:36:47,010
I'll take it.

945
00:36:47,360 --> 00:36:48,210
Good, very good.

946
00:36:48,210 --> 00:36:48,670
Put it on.

947
00:36:48,670 --> 00:36:50,670
Now, the whole family is happy.

948
00:36:50,670 --> 00:36:51,630
How wonderful.

949
00:36:51,880 --> 00:36:52,670
Put it on. This is great.

950
00:36:52,670 --> 00:36:53,430
Mom, sit down.

951
00:36:53,430 --> 00:36:53,960
Gaoyuan.

952
00:36:54,840 --> 00:36:56,280
Are we being impolite?

953
00:36:56,400 --> 00:36:57,330
What do you mean?

954
00:36:57,590 --> 00:36:58,510
Does Commander Fang

955
00:36:58,510 --> 00:36:59,280
not know

956
00:36:59,280 --> 00:37:00,810
that we are in Binjiang now?

957
00:37:00,840 --> 00:37:02,440
The two of you only invited us here

958
00:37:02,440 --> 00:37:03,360
to take photos.

959
00:37:04,800 --> 00:37:05,510
It's okay.

960
00:37:06,710 --> 00:37:07,840
My dad really doesn't know,

961
00:37:07,840 --> 00:37:09,440
since I haven't told him yet.

962
00:37:12,520 --> 00:37:14,590
But... marriage is a big deal.

963
00:37:15,030 --> 00:37:15,760
I thought...

964
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:17,170
Please don't worry.

965
00:37:17,510 --> 00:37:19,190
I make decisions about my own life.

966
00:37:19,190 --> 00:37:20,480
About him, too.

967
00:37:23,360 --> 00:37:25,070
Just don't worry. Mom.

968
00:37:28,360 --> 00:37:28,820
Come on.

969
00:37:28,880 --> 00:37:29,670
No more talking. Time for photos.

970
00:37:29,670 --> 00:37:30,270
Get ready.

971
00:37:31,800 --> 00:37:32,400
Smile.

972
00:37:32,840 --> 00:37:33,770
Please get closer.

973
00:37:33,770 --> 00:37:34,830
Look at the camera.

974
00:37:34,880 --> 00:37:35,610
This is good.

975
00:37:36,480 --> 00:37:39,030
Three, two, one!

976
00:37:42,840 --> 00:37:43,440
Here, Mom.

977
00:37:43,520 --> 00:37:44,380
Wash your feet.

978
00:37:52,920 --> 00:37:53,920
Anything wrong, Mom?

979
00:37:53,920 --> 00:37:54,550
Sit down.

980
00:38:01,320 --> 00:38:03,320
This is so unfair to you, my good boy.

981
00:38:04,190 --> 00:38:05,630
How is it unfair to me?

982
00:38:06,360 --> 00:38:07,480
Look at that girl.

983
00:38:07,630 --> 00:38:09,760
You even have to marry into her family.

984
00:38:09,840 --> 00:38:12,110
It is our fault for being impoverished.

985
00:38:15,920 --> 00:38:17,050
I know you're trying

986
00:38:17,550 --> 00:38:19,210
to climb up the social ladder.

987
00:38:19,550 --> 00:38:21,440
If you had been allowed to stay in Beijing

988
00:38:21,440 --> 00:38:23,900
back then, you could've found
a better girl.

989
00:38:24,230 --> 00:38:26,030
Mom, what are you talking about?

990
00:38:26,320 --> 00:38:28,150
She and I chose each other.

991
00:38:29,030 --> 00:38:30,630
Besides, her father is a military officer.

992
00:38:30,630 --> 00:38:31,320
I'm not a soldier.

993
00:38:31,320 --> 00:38:32,650
What can he help me with?

994
00:38:33,190 --> 00:38:34,650
Then what do you see in her?

995
00:38:35,030 --> 00:38:35,670
That girl

996
00:38:35,920 --> 00:38:37,250
is not easy to deal with.

997
00:38:37,850 --> 00:38:38,880
I like it that she teases me

998
00:38:38,880 --> 00:38:40,280
and has me wrapped around her finger.

999
00:38:40,280 --> 00:38:41,510
My goodness!

1000
00:38:43,360 --> 00:38:44,150
Did your father

1001
00:38:44,150 --> 00:38:45,400
give you your name

1002
00:38:45,400 --> 00:38:46,030
and work his tail off

1003
00:38:46,030 --> 00:38:47,880
to support you through college

1004
00:38:48,880 --> 00:38:49,630
so you could be

1005
00:38:49,630 --> 00:38:50,920
a servant to someone?

1006
00:38:52,150 --> 00:38:52,980
Is that what you think?

1007
00:38:52,980 --> 00:38:53,800
I was just joking.

1008
00:38:53,800 --> 00:38:55,130
Let's drop the subject.

1009
00:38:55,190 --> 00:38:55,920
Don't be mad.

1010
00:38:57,800 --> 00:38:58,730
I'm telling you,

1011
00:38:59,400 --> 00:39:00,800
once she marries you, she'll be

1012
00:39:00,800 --> 00:39:02,110
the Yu family's daughter-in-law.

1013
00:39:02,110 --> 00:39:03,280
I don't care if you get on top

1014
00:39:03,280 --> 00:39:04,550
of her or the other way around.

1015
00:39:04,550 --> 00:39:05,800
Just make sure you won't be

1016
00:39:05,800 --> 00:39:07,330
a disgrace to the Yu family.

1017
00:39:07,810 --> 00:39:09,080
Tame her, or I won't

1018
00:39:09,110 --> 00:39:11,040
acknowledge you as my son anymore.

1019
00:39:18,280 --> 00:39:19,080
Alright, Dad.

1020
00:39:19,320 --> 00:39:19,840
Don't be mad.

1021
00:39:19,840 --> 00:39:20,970
Dad, stop being mad.

1022
00:39:22,760 --> 00:39:24,890
You two get some rest. I'm heading out.

1023
00:39:30,000 --> 00:39:31,400
Talk some sense into him.

1024
00:39:32,910 --> 00:39:35,280
[Adjudication Committee Conference Room]

1025
00:39:33,280 --> 00:39:34,810
This is a significant case.

1026
00:39:35,440 --> 00:39:36,920
The whole city and even the province

1027
00:39:36,920 --> 00:39:38,510
are breathing down our necks.

1028
00:39:38,510 --> 00:39:39,840
Yet the collegial panel

1029
00:39:40,480 --> 00:39:42,080
failed to reach a consensus.

1030
00:39:43,360 --> 00:39:44,490
How did that happen?

1031
00:39:46,670 --> 00:39:48,960
I think the prosecution has basically

1032
00:39:49,030 --> 00:39:50,280
listed clear facts

1033
00:39:50,440 --> 00:39:51,900
and conclusive evidence.

1034
00:39:52,110 --> 00:39:53,150
By law, the accused, Qian Xingliang,

1035
00:39:53,150 --> 00:39:54,810
should be sentenced to death.

1036
00:39:55,960 --> 00:39:57,490
But Xia Yingjie disagrees.

1037
00:39:59,550 --> 00:40:00,230
In my opinion, there are

1038
00:40:00,230 --> 00:40:01,920
substantial doubts in this case.

1039
00:40:01,920 --> 00:40:03,280
Even the identity of the deceased

1040
00:40:03,280 --> 00:40:04,760
cannot be absolutely confirmed.

1041
00:40:04,760 --> 00:40:06,150
It is irresponsible to rush

1042
00:40:06,150 --> 00:40:07,030
to a verdict.

1043
00:40:09,880 --> 00:40:11,480
Although the deceased has been identified

1044
00:40:11,480 --> 00:40:12,680
through blood typing

1045
00:40:12,800 --> 00:40:14,190
and her relatives' identification,

1046
00:40:14,190 --> 00:40:15,990
neither of these is conclusive.

1047
00:40:17,030 --> 00:40:17,880
A skull superimposition test

1048
00:40:17,880 --> 00:40:19,480
has been done as well, right?

1049
00:40:19,630 --> 00:40:20,130
Right.

1050
00:40:20,590 --> 00:40:22,150
But a person's identity

1051
00:40:22,490 --> 00:40:23,630
cannot be established

1052
00:40:23,630 --> 00:40:25,480
unless the 64 indicators
in all the 4 categories

1053
00:40:25,480 --> 00:40:27,230
of the said test produce a complete match.

1054
00:40:27,230 --> 00:40:28,320
If inconsistency is found

1055
00:40:28,320 --> 00:40:29,230
in two or more indicators,

1056
00:40:29,230 --> 00:40:31,230
then the identity cannot be confirmed.

1057
00:40:31,230 --> 00:40:32,560
What's the problem now?

1058
00:40:32,590 --> 00:40:34,520
Negative match in two indicators.

1059
00:40:35,280 --> 00:40:36,150
Didn't you just say

1060
00:40:36,150 --> 00:40:37,420
the criterion was inconsistency

1061
00:40:37,420 --> 00:40:39,020
in more than two indicators?

1062
00:40:41,030 --> 00:40:42,490
I said two or more than two.

1063
00:40:43,920 --> 00:40:45,320
It's not a 100% match.

1064
00:40:45,840 --> 00:40:47,510
No case is 100% certain.

1065
00:40:50,480 --> 00:40:51,480
Another thing is,

1066
00:40:51,720 --> 00:40:52,710
the defendant's confessions

1067
00:40:52,710 --> 00:40:53,800
show a process of gradually

1068
00:40:53,800 --> 00:40:55,200
aligning with the facts.

1069
00:40:55,230 --> 00:40:56,760
I suspect he was subjected to inducement.

1070
00:40:56,760 --> 00:40:58,920
Your suspicion isn't equal to the truth.

1071
00:40:58,920 --> 00:41:00,480
Besides, there is other proof.

1072
00:41:00,480 --> 00:41:01,920
That kitchen knife counts, right?

1073
00:41:01,920 --> 00:41:03,450
But there are still doubts.

1074
00:41:04,030 --> 00:41:04,960
This murder weapon was not

1075
00:41:04,960 --> 00:41:06,190
recovered until over 10 days

1076
00:41:06,190 --> 00:41:07,550
passed after the incident.

1077
00:41:07,550 --> 00:41:08,440
Yu Sanhua's blood

1078
00:41:08,440 --> 00:41:09,710
was surprisingly still on it.

1079
00:41:09,710 --> 00:41:11,440
It's logically questionable.

1080
00:41:21,510 --> 00:41:23,920
Anything else to add?

1081
00:41:31,480 --> 00:41:32,540
Court Pres. Jiang,

1082
00:41:32,840 --> 00:41:33,510
I...

1083
00:41:33,710 --> 00:41:35,760
would like to criticize myself first.

1084
00:41:35,760 --> 00:41:37,710
Why rush for that?

1085
00:41:39,230 --> 00:41:39,960
The two of you

1086
00:41:40,480 --> 00:41:41,190
please step out.

1087
00:41:41,190 --> 00:41:42,850
We need to deliberate on this.

1088
00:41:45,440 --> 00:41:46,500
Court Pres. Jiang,

1089
00:41:46,840 --> 00:41:48,190
members of the committee,

1090
00:41:48,190 --> 00:41:49,650
I have a few remarks to add.

1091
00:41:49,850 --> 00:41:50,880
If we let a murderer walk

1092
00:41:50,880 --> 00:41:52,140
for now, there is still

1093
00:41:52,920 --> 00:41:54,850
a chance to remedy it in the future.

1094
00:41:55,230 --> 00:41:56,230
But if we take a man's life

1095
00:41:56,230 --> 00:41:57,560
for the wrong reason...

1096
00:41:59,710 --> 00:42:01,310
Save that emotional speech.

1097
00:42:01,670 --> 00:42:03,130
Please leave the room now.

1098
00:42:27,030 --> 00:42:28,190
Mei, I'm sorry.

1099
00:42:28,190 --> 00:42:29,440
Alright, say no more.

1100
00:42:30,110 --> 00:42:31,040
Maybe I'm right,

1101
00:42:31,070 --> 00:42:32,030
or maybe you are.

1102
00:42:32,030 --> 00:42:33,490
But it doesn't matter now.

1103
00:42:36,480 --> 00:42:39,140
How do you think
the committee will rule on this?

1104
00:42:40,290 --> 00:42:41,230
Court Pres. Jiang gave

1105
00:42:41,230 --> 00:42:42,550
clear hints, didn't he?

1106
00:42:42,550 --> 00:42:44,280
A death sentence, absolutely.

1107
00:42:44,280 --> 00:42:45,800
I already told you
this is a wild goose chase.

1108
00:42:45,800 --> 00:42:47,860
Now, even I am dragged into this mess.

1109
00:42:49,110 --> 00:42:49,760
What if...

1110
00:42:50,070 --> 00:42:51,470
I mean, hypothetically,

1111
00:42:51,550 --> 00:42:52,880
what if giving Qian a death sentence

1112
00:42:52,880 --> 00:42:53,800
turns out to be a mistake?

1113
00:42:53,800 --> 00:42:54,320
Xia,

1114
00:42:55,440 --> 00:42:56,630
if you're worried about

1115
00:42:56,630 --> 00:42:58,280
taking responsibility for it,

1116
00:42:58,280 --> 00:42:59,230
I can tell you for sure

1117
00:42:59,230 --> 00:43:00,000
that we will be

1118
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:01,590
both to blame.

1119
00:43:01,760 --> 00:43:02,630
Neither of us will be off the hook.
